thread:
maya: Hey — quick heads up. I noticed the Python SDK surfaces errors as typed exceptions (e.g. Error.code = "unauthenticated", status = 401) but the JS SDK sometimes returns a 403 with a freeform message "permission denied". Sample app logic that checks for error.code fails in JS.
alex: Ugh, thanks for catching. That sounds like parity drift between SDK error wrappers. What environments/requests did you see it on?
maya: Hosted API, token expired vs token valid but missing /*scope*/. Minimal repro: calling embeddings endpoint with old token in node sample app.
samir: On the server side we return 401 for invalid/expired creds and 403 when an authz check fails. Internally the error shape always has an enum code, but some internal gateways were flattening the response for certain proxies which made JS SDK parse it differently.
alex: OK. Proposed fix: standardize SDK behavior to expose both HTTP status and a normalized code string property (e.g. .status, .code) across all languages. For JS we should stop throwing opaque Error.message for auth and instead use a typed class AuthError with code set.
julia-docs: I can add a docs note in the auth troubleshooting page and a sample snippet showing robust error handling. Example snippet I want to add:

```js
try {
  await client.embed(...)
} catch (err) {
  // prefer typed fields when available
  if (err.code === 'unauthenticated' || err.status === 401) {
    // refresh token / reauth
  } else if (err.code === 'permission_denied' || err.status === 403) {
    // missing scope: surface link to console
  } else if (err.status >= 500) {
    // server error: retry with backoff
  }
}
```
maya: Nice, please include parsing for Retry-After and a short exponential backoff snippet for transient 5xxs.
alex: Agree. For immediate triage I'll open a small PR in the JS SDK to map gateway responses into our canonical error model. Assigning to me. I'll add unit tests ensuring err.code and err.status both exist.
samir: I'll check the gateway proxies and make sure they forward the structured body for auth errors. If proxies strip it we'll fallback to mapping status -> code on server before sending.
devex-bot: <link> https://internal.redwood/docs/errors#auth-shapes — pinned doc on canonical error surface. Use it for SDK parity.
maya: One more Q — do we want SDKs to expose a retryHint string for client guidance (e.g. "no-retry", "retry-after", "backoff")? Would help sample apps.
alex: I like that. Add a small schema field error.retry_hint (values: none, retry-after, idempotent-backoff). Docs + SDK PR will include mapping rules.
julia-docs: I'll update samples and add a short paragraph to onboarding that shows graceful handling and clear user-facing messages for 401 vs 403. Will link to the new JS snippet once PR lands.
maya: Awesome — thanks. Leaving a small checklist: (1) alex: SDK PR for JS mapping, (2) samir: proxy fix or server-side mapping, (3) julia-docs: sample + guide update. Ping here when done :thumbsup:

alex: Will do. ETA EOD tomorrow for PR + tests.

samir: I'll follow up in the infra channel if proxies need changes.

julia-docs: Adding TODOs to docs board now.
